This repository (Lumen attendant / pacbot-attendant) is content only:
a persona (prompt/), skill folders (skills/), a Dockerfile, and build/test
scripts. It is licensed MIT (see LICENSE).

## Base image

The Dockerfile builds `FROM` an image built locally from
plow-pbc/plow-openclaw-agent at commit 7c476de (see base.lock). That
repository has **no LICENSE file** as of that commit (checked directly;
every sibling Plow repository, plow-agents, agent-index-client,
plow-hermes-agent, life-assistant-hermes-agent, is Apache-2.0, so this
looks like an oversight rather than a deliberate choice). Because it carries
no license, nothing from its source is copied into this repository. This
repo only depends on a locally-built image tag produced from it; no Plow
source file is vendored, quoted at length, or redistributed here.

plow-openclaw-agent's own base is `ghcr.io/openclaw/openclaw`
(Apache-2.0-licensed sibling ecosystem; OpenClaw's own license governs that
image and is unaffected by anything in this repo).

## Vendored content

`skills/pacbot/` is vendored from `PacsArcade/pacbot` (MIT), via
`scripts/vendor-pacbot.sh`. See `skills/pacbot/VENDORED.md` for the exact
commit vendored and why it differs from the commit named in the hackathon
plan (a factual correction to Pac's Arcade's stated tax status, not new
content).

## Traffic and tokens

Plow relays the phone line this agent answers on and pays the model tokens
through the owner's own `PLOW_AGENT_TOKEN`. See README.md, "Who sees the
traffic."
